From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 21:21:19 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 600/604] dt-bindings: power: supply: bq25890: describe the OTG
 boost regulator

The driver registers the OTG boost as a regulator named by an
usb-otg-vbus child node, but the binding does not describe the node.
Describe it, and how it combines with linux,no-chip-config: the boost
is then the only output, and it needs the guard that keeps the chip's
watchdog fed.
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/power/supply/bq25890.yaml    | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/bq25890.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/bq25890.yaml
index a2e66d92e..b83c474ff 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/bq25890.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/bq25890.yaml
@@ -36,7 +36,8 @@ properties:
     description:
       The firmware and the chip's defaults keep the chip's configuration. The
       driver does not reset or program it, and writes only charge enable and
-      the watchdog kick. The interrupt and the ti, limits are not needed.
+      the watchdog kick, and the OTG boost enable when usb-otg-vbus is
+      present. The interrupt and the ti, limits are not needed.
 
   linux,guard-battery:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/string
@@ -55,6 +56,15 @@ properties:
       The initial charge_control_end_threshold, in percent. 100 turns the
       capacity limit off.
 
+  usb-otg-vbus:
+    $ref: /schemas/regulator/regulator.yaml#
+    unevaluatedProperties: false
+    description:
+      The OTG boost, which sources VBUS. With linux,no-chip-config it is
+      registered only when this node is present, and it needs
+      linux,guard-battery, which keeps the chip's watchdog fed while the
+      boost is on; the watchdog's expiry turns the boost off.
+
   ti,battery-regulation-voltage:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
     description: maximum charging voltage (in uV)
-- 
